  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 124 PM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nSurface high pressure will build into west Texas behind the strong \ncold front on Sunday, allowing winds to quickly subside by the \nafternoon.  High temperatures should be held down to the mid 50s \nduring the day due to cold advection.  Temperatures should recover \nrather quickly into the 60s and 70s for Monday and Tuesday as the \nsurface high moves to the east and southerly flow resumes. Looking \nahead to the middle of next week, global models are coming into \nbetter agreement on the track and intensity of the next system \nexpected to move into the western US.  For now, ensembles show low \nto medium (20-40%) chances for rain Wednesday night with this \nsystem.  This system will be monitored for the next few days as the \ntrack and intensity could easily change.",
